2
00:00:14,097 --> 00:00:21,597
<i>A Woman's Gamble / Onna no Toba / WomanGambler1 (1966)</i>

3
00:00:42,391 --> 00:00:43,531
Ready?

4
00:01:01,250 --> 00:01:01,852
All set

5
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:02,679
Okay, go ahead.

6
00:01:05,781 --> 00:01:06,711
Is that alright?

7
00:01:11,135 --> 00:01:11,921
Bid

8
00:01:16,570 --> 00:01:18,022
it's done

9
00:01:18,350 --> 00:01:19,085
Let's go ahead!

10
00:01:20,313 --> 00:01:20,914
Ready?

11
00:01:29,727 --> 00:01:30,234
5

12
00:01:58,093 --> 00:01:58,882
Ready?

13
00:02:04,172 --> 00:02:04,727
All set

14
00:02:05,055 --> 00:02:05,680
Okay, go ahead.

15
00:02:06,341 --> 00:02:07,226
Come on in

16
00:02:08,625 --> 00:02:09,578
Come on

17
00:02:11,383 --> 00:02:13,320
You guys ok?
All set.

18
00:02:13,664 --> 00:02:14,477
I'm ready.

19
00:02:14,844 --> 00:02:15,641
Here we go.

20
00:02:20,406 --> 00:02:20,953
4

21
00:02:47,835 --> 00:02:48,421
Ready?

22
00:02:50,641 --> 00:02:51,375
All set.

23
00:02:51,867 --> 00:02:52,845
please make it

24
00:02:52,870 --> 00:02:54,039
Okay, go ahead?

25
00:02:54,064 --> 00:02:55,735
Are you ready? Go ahead,

26
00:02:55,760 --> 00:02:56,710
Okay

27
00:02:57,219 --> 00:02:57,852
Are you ready?

28
00:02:57,888 --> 00:02:59,109
We made it.

29
00:02:59,134 --> 00:02:59,797
Ready?

30
00:03:08,031 --> 00:03:08,985
Wait!

31
00:03:15,633 --> 00:03:17,992
There's a doubt about this

32
00:03:18,705 --> 00:03:21,898
Hey young man,
What do you mean?

33
00:03:23,571 --> 00:03:25,008
Should I say that clearly?

34
00:03:25,570 --> 00:03:28,429
You speak indirectly, don't you?

35
00:03:29,220 --> 00:03:32,625
Are you trying to pick a fight with me, customer?

36
00:03:33,101 --> 00:03:35,570
I don't know if you're from katori group or whatever, but...

37
00:03:36,290 --> 00:03:40,843
This is a gathering of prominent figures from
the Kanto Kyoyukai, all enjoying themselves

38
00:03:41,570 --> 00:03:43,156
Don't talk to me like that

39
00:03:45,843 --> 00:03:48,843
You might find it annoying while you're playing.

40
00:03:49,577 --> 00:03:53,211
but I can't just stand by.
I, too, am a gambler.

41
00:03:53,607 --> 00:03:57,686
Do you think we're involved in match-fixing?

42
00:03:59,508 --> 00:04:00,445
You're absolutely right.

43
00:04:00,617 --> 00:04:01,133
What?

44
00:04:01,158 --> 00:04:01,672
Masa

45
00:04:02,055 --> 00:04:02,711
But...

46
00:04:02,900 --> 00:04:03,706
Stay down

47
00:04:07,557 --> 00:04:10,304
Young man, we aren't calm

48
00:04:11,459 --> 00:04:13,705
On what grounds do you think we're fixing matches?

49
00:04:15,625 --> 00:04:17,890
Your companion is using their left hand to signal you.

50
00:04:18,947 --> 00:04:22,616
That person is Tsukada,you

51
00:04:23,555 --> 00:04:25,078
You're an idiot.

52
00:04:27,511 --> 00:04:29,780
He is signaling the number three to you.

53
00:04:31,900 --> 00:04:32,664
Right?

54
00:04:33,675 --> 00:04:35,109
Tsukada also bet on 3.

55
00:04:35,941 --> 00:04:37,101
and that's all I want to say

56
00:04:37,659 --> 00:04:40,015
What's the hell.
Give the money back.

57
00:04:40,040 --> 00:04:40,906
What's the fuck.

58
00:04:40,931 --> 00:04:42,719
Don't take us for fools.

59
00:04:42,744 --> 00:04:43,852
Please be quiet!

60
00:04:46,304 --> 00:04:51,367
Tatsuzo is a comrade who has lived his
life for 40 years as a master in this field

61
00:04:52,770 --> 00:04:54,929
There's no way they'd be rigging a match

62
00:04:55,810 --> 00:04:59,211
The signal using cigarette ash is truly a masterful technique

63
00:05:00,007 --> 00:05:02,828
I hear you're from katori

64
00:05:04,106 --> 00:05:08,039
I am Tachibana Tesuji, a managing director at the Katori-gumi.

65
00:05:08,064 --> 00:05:08,714
Tachibana?

66
00:05:09,665 --> 00:05:16,745
If this turns out not to be a fixed match, how will you take responsibility?

67
00:05:24,740 --> 00:05:28,940
My body is filthy, but please feel free to treat me

68
00:05:30,780 --> 00:05:32,807
You are young, but you have guts.

69
00:05:33,567 --> 00:05:38,846
What would you do if the number 3 came up, just as he said?

70
00:05:39,350 --> 00:05:43,917
I will take responsibility for this situation.

71
00:05:45,171 --> 00:05:48,580
I will settle this matter in the name of the Kanematsu Group

72
00:05:49,250 --> 00:05:54,354
Boss, let me take care of the matter that came up

73
00:05:55,605 --> 00:05:56,441
Tatsu.

74
00:05:58,985 --> 00:06:01,985
Now, please open that card.

75
00:06:03,460 --> 00:06:06,460
Tsukada,Are you ready?

76
00:06:08,330 --> 00:06:09,198
Yes

77
00:06:35,909 --> 00:06:38,276
Two and three!
This isn't a fix.

78
00:06:45,476 --> 00:06:46,401
The young ones!

79
00:06:47,301 --> 00:06:50,003
You did something really stupid.

80
00:07:04,347 --> 00:07:05,620
Look at this

81
00:07:07,605 --> 00:07:08,511
Fixed game

82
00:07:09,702 --> 00:07:13,120
You are not professionals.

83
00:07:41,175 --> 00:07:41,824
Welcome back.

84
00:07:46,399 --> 00:07:48,625
It's raining heavily, isn't it?

85
00:07:48,689 --> 00:07:50,214
It's very cold today, isn't it?

86
00:07:50,239 --> 00:07:51,464
I will prepare some alcohol for you.

87
00:07:51,652 --> 00:07:52,730
Water is fine

88
00:07:56,473 --> 00:07:58,088
How was the Hanafuda event?

89
00:07:58,254 --> 00:08:00,040
it was magnificent!

90
00:08:00,080 --> 00:08:01,542
A lot of famous people came.

91
00:08:02,255 --> 00:08:05,255
An event like that is very rare.

92
00:08:06,183 --> 00:08:10,173
It was an annual gathering for people from the Kyoyu group.

93
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:14,557
You are the only one who can handle the situation.

94
00:08:14,987 --> 00:08:16,456
Shall we grill some chicken?

95
00:08:16,481 --> 00:08:17,355
No problem

96
00:08:23,753 --> 00:08:27,394
It's a good thing you left the world of the yakuza.

97
00:08:29,200 --> 00:08:31,908
I know it's all thanks to Kanematsu-san.

98
00:08:34,402 --> 00:08:35,847
I know

99
00:08:36,036 --> 00:08:39,036
I wonder where Hiroshi is right now?

100
00:08:39,810 --> 00:08:44,011
I think he is away on a school trip to Kagoshima.

101
00:08:44,580 --> 00:08:47,580
He's going to university next year

102
00:08:48,190 --> 00:08:49,386
He's a boy after all

103
00:08:49,410 --> 00:08:51,816
He'll be looked down upon if he doesn't have a university degree

104
00:08:51,840 --> 00:08:53,756
If only this store were to thrive

105
00:08:53,780 --> 00:08:56,780
He'll probably be able to make a living even if he goes to university

106
00:08:57,572 --> 00:09:01,612
Mr. Kanematsu's father just won't raise the rent

107
00:09:02,019 --> 00:09:02,940
It's a real problem.

108
00:09:03,042 --> 00:09:07,917
He is enabling you to live in the ordinary human world for very low rent.

109
00:09:09,194 --> 00:09:12,194
I know you must never forget Mr. Kanematsu's kindness.

110
00:09:15,905 --> 00:09:16,342
Aki.

111
00:09:17,547 --> 00:09:19,311
Are things going well with Moriya?

112
00:09:23,147 --> 00:09:26,147
I would like to do something to help you too

113
00:09:26,331 --> 00:09:29,097
So we're planning to get married once Hiroshi gets into university

114
00:09:29,130 --> 00:09:32,130
I see.
He's a good guy

115
00:09:32,569 --> 00:09:34,428
But we'll have to make some money for a while,

116
00:09:34,453 --> 00:09:35,209
so is it all over now?

117
00:09:35,234 --> 00:09:37,233
I'm really tired today

118
00:09:39,428 --> 00:09:41,178
I still haven't prepared your bed.

119
00:09:41,203 --> 00:09:42,225
Don’t worry.
I will do it myself.

120
00:10:32,508 --> 00:10:33,537
Dad!

121
00:10:35,460 --> 00:10:36,546
Dad!

122
00:10:41,788 --> 00:10:42,530
Dad...

123
00:11:07,099 --> 00:11:08,334
Our father was an idiot

124
00:11:11,158 --> 00:11:12,022
Hiroshi

125
00:11:13,585 --> 00:11:15,186
There's no need to commit suicide.

126
00:11:16,393 --> 00:11:19,393
It's so old-fashioned, so very old-fashioned.

127
00:11:20,771 --> 00:11:23,560
Our father couldn't live without bon

128
00:11:24,028 --> 00:11:29,037
Then why did he cheat? If he has enough
pride, he should have refused

129
00:11:31,483 --> 00:11:32,655
Masakichi.

130
00:11:33,264 --> 00:11:36,281
What exactly was Tsukada's sense of obligation?

131
00:11:37,310 --> 00:11:39,022
I don't really understand it either

132
00:11:39,530 --> 00:11:41,716
When his older sister passed away the year before last

133
00:11:41,756 --> 00:11:46,077
He got Kashimoto to cover the cost of that money.

134
00:11:47,021 --> 00:11:49,858
Why didn't he consult the boss of Kanematsu about that?

135
00:11:51,545 --> 00:11:55,628
especially since the Kanematsu group was in chaos
after a major conflict with the Iwata family

136
00:11:55,660 --> 00:11:58,850
I think your father was probably hesitant to ask

137
00:11:59,660 --> 00:12:01,412
If it's money he borrowed, just pay it back, right?

138
00:12:02,264 --> 00:12:05,405
Mr. Kanematsu would understand if he talked to him about it

139
00:12:05,586 --> 00:12:08,586
Well, it would be easy to say that,

140
00:12:09,116 --> 00:12:13,608
but our father is the kind of person who will uphold his principles even if it means ruining himself

141
00:12:14,850 --> 00:12:18,827
Even though he knew it was a fix, he couldn't say so in front of the crowd.

142
00:12:19,522 --> 00:12:25,035
I was really impressed by Tachibana's spirit to try and settle things once and for all by putting his life on the line.

143
00:12:26,177 --> 00:12:26,942
I'm afraid

144
00:12:27,090 --> 00:12:29,206
That matter also

145
00:12:29,230 --> 00:12:36,497
As a result of the board meeting, it was decided that Kanematsu and Tachibana would switch places as board members of the Kyoyukai

146
00:12:37,970 --> 00:12:41,637
The reason the previous chairman organized the Kashimoto throughout the Kanto region

147
00:12:41,701 --> 00:12:47,794
and created the Kyoyukai was because he felt that it wasn't enough to just fight amongst themselves over territory

148
00:12:48,169 --> 00:12:51,551
it was time to expand their business outwards

149
00:12:52,900 --> 00:12:55,900
We need talented young people like you to grow and improve

150
00:12:56,840 --> 00:12:59,840
we can't rest in peace if you're not with us

151
00:13:00,645 --> 00:13:01,622
You think so,right

152
00:13:03,225 --> 00:13:04,551
You're absolutely right.

153
00:13:06,250 --> 00:13:08,186
Thank you for understanding.

154
00:13:08,210 --> 00:13:11,905
I am too young, so I don't know if I can do that.

155
00:13:13,510 --> 00:13:18,583
In this day and age, the yakuza won't survive unless both the newcomers and the veterans work together

156
00:13:21,870 --> 00:13:23,137
Don't worry

157
00:13:23,741 --> 00:13:25,848
As long as I'm here, you don't need to worry.

158
00:13:27,154 --> 00:13:28,090
But...

159
00:13:28,388 --> 00:13:31,223
Kanematsu readily agreed

160
00:13:31,799 --> 00:13:33,544
There's no need to hold back any further.

161
00:13:34,638 --> 00:13:36,497
I'm impressed you're saying that much

162
00:13:37,146 --> 00:13:37,966
Please let me do that.

163
00:13:38,501 --> 00:13:40,489
The feet are fine, so that settles it

164
00:13:41,712 --> 00:13:45,527
But Daigashi would be bad to have a substitute executive in place of Kanematsu, wouldn't it?

165
00:13:47,060 --> 00:13:47,849
What do you think?

166
00:13:48,460 --> 00:13:51,176
I'll talk to Katori about it

167
00:13:51,949 --> 00:13:56,278
Why don't you break away from the Katori-gumi and form the Tachibana-gumi?

168
00:13:57,421 --> 00:13:59,020
I have nothing to say

169
00:14:01,687 --> 00:14:03,981
I leave everything to you.

170
00:14:05,504 --> 00:14:09,731
They were arrested for gambling at a hot spring.

171
00:14:09,764 --> 00:14:12,153
Police enforcement has been strict lately.

172
00:14:13,421 --> 00:14:16,421
What will you talk about in the middle of the day?

173
00:14:17,712 --> 00:14:19,887
Welcome back

174
00:14:23,857 --> 00:14:24,583
Hey.

175
00:14:25,302 --> 00:14:27,832
You has a visitor upstairs

176
00:14:29,530 --> 00:14:33,364
I have no reason to accept such a large amount of condolence money from you

177
00:14:34,270 --> 00:14:38,012
I have no intention of being so stingy as to try to
atone for my sins with such a small amount of money

178
00:14:40,972 --> 00:14:42,886
Well, you can use it to help pay for building a tombstone

179
00:14:42,997 --> 00:14:44,316
That's not good.

180
00:14:44,966 --> 00:14:47,966
It's my father and Mr. Tsukada's fault for setting up the whole scheme in the first place

181
00:14:49,800 --> 00:14:51,872
Tatsuo had a dignified end

182
00:14:52,247 --> 00:14:54,941
Not a single person in my group speaks ill of him.

183
00:14:56,040 --> 00:14:58,192
Tatsuzo's name will live on proudly

184
00:15:01,290 --> 00:15:03,598
Is it the pride of a gambler?

185
00:15:04,964 --> 00:15:07,871
I was very impressed by that.

186
00:15:10,418 --> 00:15:13,965
I regret that I acted childishly

187
00:15:16,007 --> 00:15:20,075
I am deeply saddened by the loss of my colleague.

188
00:15:21,040 --> 00:15:25,434
I never imagined Ms. Tachibana would think that way

189
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:29,286
And that reserve Tsukada guy practically ran
away to Osaka in the middle of the night,

190
00:15:30,570 --> 00:15:32,309
He tarnished a gambler's pride.

191
00:15:35,142 --> 00:15:38,707
Well, he probably won't be able to show his face at the Kyoyukai ever again

192
00:15:38,950 --> 00:15:41,145
You have a call from Mr. Bond

193
00:15:41,833 --> 00:15:42,973
Tell him to do it later

194
00:15:42,998 --> 00:15:44,804
You could at least answer the phone, couldn't you?

195
00:15:45,140 --> 00:15:47,496
You idiot! What a mouth you've got

196
00:15:47,520 --> 00:15:48,864
Excuse me

197
00:15:49,010 --> 00:15:50,137
No, no, don't worry about it

198
00:15:51,108 --> 00:15:52,512
How long are you going to stand there

199
00:15:57,550 --> 00:16:00,325
I decided not to show my face at the funeral

200
00:16:01,309 --> 00:16:04,973
The thought of you and your father being left
behind makes me feel terrible when I sleep

201
00:16:07,271 --> 00:16:08,208
What do you think?

202
00:16:08,911 --> 00:16:12,107
Would you let me take care of you guys?

203
00:16:13,610 --> 00:16:18,231
Even Kanematsu-san, unlike in the past, is now completely preoccupied with managing the gang's finances

204
00:16:19,250 --> 00:16:21,309
He's not going to take care of all of you

205
00:16:24,375 --> 00:16:28,264
If we expand and increase our workforce, our income
will double

206
00:16:31,366 --> 00:16:33,662
and if that improves your lives,

207
00:16:34,130 --> 00:16:35,976
I'll feel a little more at ease

208
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:39,545
We are fine with our current lifestyle.

209
00:16:40,350 --> 00:16:42,967
I've come to accept that my father's passing was simply unfortunate

210
00:16:43,390 --> 00:16:45,136
Please don't worry about it too much.

211
00:16:45,161 --> 00:16:46,373
, and try to forget about it

212
00:16:48,170 --> 00:16:50,342
Anyway, I'll give this back to you

213
00:16:51,600 --> 00:16:53,279
Well then, excuse me

214
00:16:59,694 --> 00:17:01,139
Welcome.

215
00:17:02,967 --> 00:17:03,327
Hi

216
00:17:04,350 --> 00:17:05,467
Welcome.

217
00:17:07,498 --> 00:17:08,725
Welcome.

218
00:17:08,750 --> 00:17:09,811
Hi

219
00:17:09,990 --> 00:17:11,498
How about a drink?

220
00:17:11,647 --> 00:17:12,973
Please hand him the glass.

221
00:17:13,350 --> 00:17:16,098
Please don't let him drink too much, Moriya-san

222
00:17:16,273 --> 00:17:17,239
What are you talking about?

223
00:17:17,264 --> 00:17:18,942
I am helping your shop.

224
00:17:20,801 --> 00:17:22,496
I'm leaving

225
00:17:24,198 --> 00:17:25,809
Tome-chan, Please give me some snacks.

226
00:17:25,872 --> 00:17:26,911
I get it.

227
00:17:29,364 --> 00:17:31,184
Come watch rugby practice tomorrow

228
00:17:31,209 --> 00:17:32,370
Do you train the athletes rigorously?

229
00:17:32,395 --> 00:17:33,047
 Don't be ridiculous!

230
00:17:33,079 --> 00:17:34,839
I'm giving up my Sunday!

231
00:17:35,582 --> 00:17:37,090
I make them work hard before their matches.

232
00:17:37,418 --> 00:17:38,809
What a scary senior...

233
00:17:39,498 --> 00:17:42,762
When it comes to rugby, your eyes light up

234
00:17:43,599 --> 00:17:48,067
I may be low-ranking at my company, but I seem to be the boss at my rugby club.

235
00:17:48,660 --> 00:17:51,955
I have a ticket to a play that a customer gave me

236
00:17:53,723 --> 00:17:55,184
Did you make an appointment with the customer?

237
00:17:55,289 --> 00:17:57,418
No, just me

238
00:17:57,699 --> 00:17:58,705
Then, come on over

239
00:17:58,730 --> 00:18:00,020
You don't have anything to do, right?

240
00:18:01,200 --> 00:18:04,137
You should go there with the intention of sunbathing.

241
00:18:04,928 --> 00:18:06,008
That's right

242
00:18:07,625 --> 00:18:09,521
Can I take Hiroshi along with me?

243
00:18:09,770 --> 00:18:10,442
Okay

244
00:18:11,016 --> 00:18:14,941
Aki-chan, you're supposed to go on a date alone

245
00:18:24,989 --> 00:18:26,395
Run hard!

246
00:18:35,216 --> 00:18:36,223
Damn it.

247
00:18:39,317 --> 00:18:41,340
Run hard!

248
00:18:44,497 --> 00:18:45,145
I am going home.

249
00:18:45,622 --> 00:18:46,302
Why?

250
00:18:47,223 --> 00:18:48,552
I have something to do.

251
00:18:50,458 --> 00:18:52,075
Hold on.

252
00:18:52,762 --> 00:18:53,794
Do you have a money with you?

253
00:18:54,216 --> 00:18:55,270
Yes I have.

254
00:18:55,589 --> 00:18:56,926
What time are you going home?

255
00:18:57,661 --> 00:18:58,356
 I don't know

256
00:19:08,914 --> 00:19:10,390
Keep going.

257
00:19:59,576 --> 00:20:03,124
Oh, are you going to make another new model?

258
00:20:03,469 --> 00:20:06,469
Yes, this time we'll make a marine weather observation sensor

259
00:20:06,862 --> 00:20:15,547
It's 75.2 meters long, 12 meters wide, and weighs 1598 gross tons, and it's attracting
global attention for its technology, including its doomsday device and active radar

260
00:20:17,840 --> 00:20:20,396
Yes, that's our dream

261
00:20:20,420 --> 00:20:22,636
It's about building nuclear-powered ships in Japan

262
00:20:22,661 --> 00:20:25,367
Oh, that's great

263
00:20:28,798 --> 00:20:30,368
It's fine, I'll do it.

264
00:20:30,630 --> 00:20:31,735
Let's hang it

265
00:20:31,884 --> 00:20:32,313
Don’t worry.

266
00:20:32,493 --> 00:20:33,295
that smelly

267
00:20:33,320 --> 00:20:34,416
I'll wash it later

268
00:20:34,440 --> 00:20:35,356
Then I'll wash it

269
00:20:35,380 --> 00:20:35,986
No, it's fine,

270
00:20:36,010 --> 00:20:37,086
I'll wash it

271
00:20:37,110 --> 00:20:38,096
I'll wash it for you

272
00:20:38,120 --> 00:20:38,996
No, I'll wash it

273
00:20:39,020 --> 00:20:40,806
I'll wash it

274
00:20:40,830 --> 00:20:42,297
Are you okay?

275
00:21:02,377 --> 00:21:03,547
I'll make you some coffee.

276
00:21:14,204 --> 00:21:17,070
Oh, and about the ship

277
00:21:17,460 --> 00:21:18,375
Tell me more

278
00:21:18,415 --> 00:21:19,907
You're quite unique

279
00:21:20,440 --> 00:21:23,071
Girls aren't usually very interested in these kinds of stories

280
00:21:24,022 --> 00:21:26,328
Even I find it difficult and don't really understand it

281
00:21:27,381 --> 00:21:32,164
But I really like how Moriya-san
with dreams for your work

282
00:21:33,423 --> 00:21:36,423
Perhaps it's because it's completely different from the world I grew up in

283
00:21:37,370 --> 00:21:39,696
But if we were born as the same human being

284
00:21:39,720 --> 00:21:46,344
I sincerely wish I could live
with dreams and pride like you do

285
00:21:46,976 --> 00:21:54,656
So... unless we somehow manage to win back the customers that the Tachibana group has taken, we won't be opening the doors to Kanematsu

286
00:21:56,231 --> 00:22:01,117
If you sits on the Bon, we can bring back our regular customers

287
00:22:03,491 --> 00:22:09,016
There is no way to win back the late boss's customers other than through you.

288
00:22:11,493 --> 00:22:17,670
Also, please do it until the Kanematsu Group recovers

289
00:22:19,163 --> 00:22:20,077
Please.

290
00:22:22,194 --> 00:22:25,327
As you can see, no matter how much it's for the Kanematsu-gumi,

291
00:22:25,604 --> 00:22:28,358
I can't sit on the Bon without telling the boss

292
00:22:29,060 --> 00:22:34,491
Besides, I don't want to go back to gambling, even for a short time

293
00:22:35,679 --> 00:22:36,320
Young lady

294
00:22:37,491 --> 00:22:38,475
I'm sorry

295
00:22:39,377 --> 00:22:42,794
You might think that a gambler's daughter is being arrogant, but

296
00:22:43,840 --> 00:22:46,840
I want to continue living an ordinary life like this

297
00:22:47,630 --> 00:22:50,741
I want to marry an ordinary person
and create a normal family

298
00:22:52,300 --> 00:22:55,300
I wonder if you can understand how I feel?

299
00:22:57,520 --> 00:22:59,975
I was wrong

300
00:23:00,619 --> 00:23:04,022
I wasn't thinking about your future.

301
00:23:04,092 --> 00:23:05,061
Don’t worry.

302
00:23:05,290 --> 00:23:06,327
I'm the one who can't be of any help,

303
00:23:06,352 --> 00:23:07,296
no, not at all

304
00:23:08,048 --> 00:23:11,048
I like gambling more than food

305
00:23:11,718 --> 00:23:12,554
So I'm sorry

306
00:23:15,678 --> 00:23:18,850
why can't I understand women's feelings at all?

307
00:23:20,200 --> 00:23:21,647
I am such an idiot!

308
00:23:25,100 --> 00:23:29,155
You've been going to the club early lately, haven't you?

309
00:23:29,850 --> 00:23:32,944
I am busy because the shop has just opened.

310
00:23:33,140 --> 00:23:34,272
What are you talking about?

311
00:23:34,804 --> 00:23:36,491
You want to see Sally soon, don't you?

312
00:23:37,147 --> 00:23:39,968
I know you're being nice to the new woman.

313
00:23:40,537 --> 00:23:41,327
Shut up!

314
00:23:41,900 --> 00:23:43,856
If you have time to line up your houses, you should be focusing on your business!

315
00:23:43,880 --> 00:23:46,155
I'm just an employee anyway

316
00:23:46,550 --> 00:23:50,131
Why? You're putting me in with some stripper-type dancer?

317
00:23:50,712 --> 00:23:52,389
If you don't like it, you can leave this place

318
00:23:54,530 --> 00:23:56,530
Hmph, what are you talking about?

319
00:23:57,003 --> 00:23:58,079
You are merely a product of hereditary succession.

320
00:24:08,138 --> 00:24:10,397
Tachibana is cool

321
00:24:10,890 --> 00:24:12,405
He's got a cool

322
00:24:12,437 --> 00:24:13,568
He is every bit the businessman.

323
00:24:13,930 --> 00:24:16,264
I heard he opened a huge nightclub in Ginza

324
00:24:16,716 --> 00:24:18,889
Wow, a yakuza running a nightclub?

325
00:24:19,135 --> 00:24:21,662
He's more like a businessman than a
yakuza,

326
00:24:21,921 --> 00:24:25,350
It wouldn't be surprising if he graduated from university and became a salaried employee.

327
00:24:25,440 --> 00:24:28,889
He might take a packed train and do grueling work.

328
00:24:29,260 --> 00:24:32,166
It's not worth it if you can't even make 1000 yen a day

329
00:24:32,190 --> 00:24:34,726
Wouldn't it be better if you guys joined the Tachibana group too?

330
00:24:34,750 --> 00:24:38,623
That company doesn't care about educational background or entrance exams.

331
00:24:41,936 --> 00:24:43,069
Hey

332
00:24:46,220 --> 00:24:48,241
How's Hiroshi's sister doing?

333
00:24:49,195 --> 00:24:51,944
Your sister came here to visit the president the other day,

334
00:24:51,969 --> 00:24:52,965
huh? my sister?

335
00:24:53,760 --> 00:24:55,811
And Mama was really desperate about it

336
00:24:55,920 --> 00:24:57,295
I got fed up.

337
00:24:57,415 --> 00:24:58,631
Hey Sub-chan, huh?

338
00:24:58,890 --> 00:25:01,592
I have something to tell you, come on over

339
00:25:07,363 --> 00:25:10,363
Me..your mom....

340
00:25:13,163 --> 00:25:14,444
Don't take it personally

341
00:25:23,968 --> 00:25:27,804
He acts all high and mighty even though he keeps failing his classes.

342
00:25:28,492 --> 00:25:31,373
I feel like I've never had a moment of pure satisfaction.

343
00:25:31,718 --> 00:25:33,803
Shall we rent a sports car and go for a drive?

344
00:25:34,168 --> 00:25:37,168
On Route 3, we can reach speeds of 120 km/h.

345
00:25:38,499 --> 00:25:39,858
Excuse me.

346
00:25:41,684 --> 00:25:43,514
Thank you for your work.

347
00:25:47,250 --> 00:25:48,816
Kanematsu's boss

348
00:25:48,840 --> 00:25:51,405
I haven't seen him for a whole

349
00:25:51,659 --> 00:25:53,850
I guess he's not feeling well after all

350
00:25:54,614 --> 00:25:56,560
I heard he need to rest

351
00:25:56,585 --> 00:25:58,311
I hope he gets well soon

352
00:26:00,687 --> 00:26:07,702
lately there are these Tachibana gang thugs walking around this neighborhood acting all high and mighty

353
00:26:08,300 --> 00:26:11,053
There's no point in you getting so anxious, you know,

354
00:26:11,186 --> 00:26:13,038
What's the hell?

355
00:26:13,710 --> 00:26:19,303
I, too, used to be a very famous woman,Otoyo Hayate.

356
00:26:19,959 --> 00:26:24,053
I get it, I get it, let's just get ready to go home,

357
00:26:24,086 --> 00:26:25,725
let's go home, let's go home

358
00:26:25,750 --> 00:26:27,108
I need to pee

359
00:26:31,180 --> 00:26:32,596
It's that thing every night,

360
00:26:32,620 --> 00:26:34,827
so I'm getting sick of it

361
00:26:35,019 --> 00:26:36,915
You married her because you love her, didn't you?

362
00:26:36,947 --> 00:26:38,748
I'm not kidding

363
00:26:38,920 --> 00:26:40,316
She's a schemer wife

364
00:26:40,340 --> 00:26:41,424
Did you say something?

365
00:26:41,448 --> 00:26:42,608
I didn't say anything

366
00:26:47,740 --> 00:26:48,755
What's wrong?

367
00:26:49,342 --> 00:26:50,956
You are drinking too much alcohol.

368
00:26:50,980 --> 00:26:52,336
Shut up.

369
00:26:52,360 --> 00:26:55,360
Give me some water, give me some water!

370
00:27:08,944 --> 00:27:10,765
What's wrong?

371
00:27:11,765 --> 00:27:12,843
I want to sleep.

372
00:27:20,929 --> 00:27:23,905
You seem to be in a very good mood.

373
00:27:26,848 --> 00:27:29,848
I wonder what's bothering that child so much that he's running around playing?

374
00:27:30,186 --> 00:27:32,647
There's nothing to worry about

375
00:27:33,130 --> 00:27:35,373
That age, you know

376
00:27:35,781 --> 00:27:40,217
They are very dissatisfied with the world.

377
00:27:41,230 --> 00:27:44,230
Eventually, he feels it is very ridiculous.

378
00:27:45,420 --> 00:27:48,420
You've been drinking since I was younger than him

379
00:27:48,490 --> 00:27:50,056
Thank you for your hard work, Otome-san

380
00:27:50,080 --> 00:27:50,991
You can go home now

381
00:27:51,016 --> 00:27:53,944
Thanks, sit down first, sit down,

382
00:29:12,952 --> 00:29:14,842
Well then, take care of yourself.

383
00:29:15,610 --> 00:29:17,296
Excuse me. first

384
00:29:18,812 --> 00:29:21,812
Come again when you have some free time,

385
00:29:26,194 --> 00:29:27,444
Give me a back massage

386
00:29:30,029 --> 00:29:35,959
Oh, he must have been devastated to find out that Tatsuzo,
who had cared for him since he was little

387
00:29:36,409 --> 00:29:38,717
He treated me really well

388
00:29:39,251 --> 00:29:41,009
Is the shop doing well?

389
00:29:41,034 --> 00:29:46,975
Yes, thankfully. It seems that Otome-san is
eager to see your healthy face soon

390
00:29:47,790 --> 00:29:54,912
I haven't eaten his cooking in ages, and even though I'm not old enough to die yet, I just haven't been able to eat it since then

391
00:29:55,426 --> 00:29:57,436
How do you feel about being hospitalized?

392
00:29:58,242 --> 00:29:59,866
That's not going to work

393
00:30:01,113 --> 00:30:07,467
That bastard Tachibana is using
Senba's backing to do whatever he wants

394
00:30:08,983 --> 00:30:13,372
They have absolutely no sense of obligation or humanity whatsoever

395
00:30:14,510 --> 00:30:16,886
No matter how young people are these days,

396
00:30:16,910 --> 00:30:18,514
there are still rules of honor and code of conduct in this world

397
00:30:19,020 --> 00:30:21,056
I wonder why they suddenly rose to prominence

398
00:30:21,088 --> 00:30:23,225
It seems like that outburst at the Hanafuda party

399
00:30:23,250 --> 00:30:26,116
It all started with a fight there.

400
00:30:27,270 --> 00:30:30,952
They had risen to power by stepping on the misfortunes of others

401
00:30:32,590 --> 00:30:35,506
I don't know if they're modern-day yakuza or whatever,

402
00:30:35,530 --> 00:30:37,397
but I could never be guys like that

403
00:30:38,333 --> 00:30:44,787
Actually, the Tachibana group acquired the land around Tatsunoya

404
00:30:45,632 --> 00:30:46,593
Tachibana?

405
00:30:47,341 --> 00:30:49,998
That land is mortgaged

406
00:30:50,220 --> 00:30:53,220
He probably ripped them off for practically nothing,

407
00:30:53,870 --> 00:30:55,446
but I wonder what their intentions were

408
00:30:55,470 --> 00:30:57,873
He came to me saying they wanted to buy the Tatsuno family home

409
00:30:59,274 --> 00:31:01,037
Of course I refused

410
00:31:02,147 --> 00:31:03,241
Then

411
00:31:03,910 --> 00:31:06,486
He's being very aggressive and demanding we move out

412
00:31:07,491 --> 00:31:09,166
If I tell my husband about it,

413
00:31:09,197 --> 00:31:11,530
He might have another heart attack

414
00:31:12,840 --> 00:31:14,655
What should I do?

415
00:31:15,060 --> 00:31:17,217
I was just having a headache

416
00:31:20,940 --> 00:31:23,940
I'll try to meet with Tachibana

417
00:31:24,430 --> 00:31:28,256
I see, but Aki-chan is alone....

418
00:31:28,870 --> 00:31:30,655
If you take Masakichi with you,

419
00:31:31,131 --> 00:31:33,436
That guy is completely useless at negotiations

420
00:31:33,720 --> 00:31:35,178
I wonder...

421
00:31:35,950 --> 00:31:39,452
He seems surprisingly reliable when he's sitting on the Bon, though

422
00:31:40,680 --> 00:31:43,280
I'll meet with him tonight

423
00:31:44,590 --> 00:31:49,342
Please accept this money,

424
00:31:49,650 --> 00:31:51,045
I'm sorry

425
00:31:51,590 --> 00:31:54,590
Besides the rent, you're doing all this for me

426
00:31:54,882 --> 00:31:59,260
No, I should be the one thanking you for letting me do business with you at such a low rent

427
00:31:59,810 --> 00:32:04,467
I’d like to show my appreciation to you during months with high sales.

428
00:32:05,300 --> 00:32:11,608
I'll keep this a secret from my family, but I'll gratefully accept it

429
00:32:15,789 --> 00:32:21,952
It seems like the Kanematsu Group has finally reached its limit

430
00:32:23,270 --> 00:32:25,178
If they were to take Tatsunoya away from them...

431
00:32:26,410 --> 00:32:28,702
this house will be the only one left

432
00:32:34,660 --> 00:32:37,660
Why the grumpy face?

433
00:32:38,780 --> 00:32:40,786
I'm kind of fed up with you

434
00:32:41,420 --> 00:32:43,810
Young people don't have to say like that.

435
00:32:44,180 --> 00:32:45,996
How long are you going to stay single?

436
00:32:46,020 --> 00:32:48,420
That is why you have that look on your face.

437
00:32:48,723 --> 00:32:49,909
Are you sexually frustrated?

438
00:32:49,990 --> 00:32:51,553
Shut up and leave me alone

439
00:32:51,710 --> 00:32:54,155
Hey you, Tome

440
00:32:55,811 --> 00:32:56,686
Tome

441
00:32:57,171 --> 00:32:59,577
Water, water, water!

442
00:33:00,069 --> 00:33:01,265
water!

443
00:33:01,290 --> 00:33:03,428
You need some water

444
00:33:03,830 --> 00:33:05,084
He is always spacing out.

445
00:33:05,151 --> 00:33:06,787
Here it is

446
00:33:15,867 --> 00:33:20,092
This is just ordinary water; it's not alcohol.

447
00:33:23,170 --> 00:33:27,920
I've been meaning to ask you this for a while,

448
00:33:28,345 --> 00:33:29,405
what is it?

449
00:33:29,467 --> 00:33:30,795
Do you love Aki-chan?

450
00:33:31,385 --> 00:33:33,381
Idiot! Don't say such stupid things!

451
00:34:02,621 --> 00:34:04,371
They're all idiots.

452
00:34:04,785 --> 00:34:06,152
Did they do it again?

453
00:34:08,003 --> 00:34:09,351
so visit them.

454
00:34:10,196 --> 00:34:11,777
Okay, I'll go

455
00:34:20,082 --> 00:34:20,723
Hi

456
00:34:22,099 --> 00:34:23,405
I've been waiting for you

457
00:34:23,430 --> 00:34:26,356
I apologize for my rudeness the other day

458
00:34:26,380 --> 00:34:29,380
Well then, Please come this way.

459
00:34:48,070 --> 00:34:50,941
Have you been wondering how things are going?

460
00:34:52,280 --> 00:34:53,691
Is Tatsunoya doing well?

461
00:34:55,472 --> 00:34:56,605
what about Tachibana-san?

462
00:34:57,543 --> 00:34:58,418
Is something the matter?

463
00:35:00,050 --> 00:35:03,433
Actually, I came here because I wanted to talk to you about that

464
00:35:03,880 --> 00:35:07,876
I hear you told Mr. Kanemoto to vacate Tatsunoya.

465
00:35:07,900 --> 00:35:10,626
Oh, if that's the case,

466
00:35:10,650 --> 00:35:12,855
then there's nothing to worry about

467
00:35:13,300 --> 00:35:15,856
You can just keep the store going as before

468
00:35:15,880 --> 00:35:18,656
I don't intend to charge rent

469
00:35:18,680 --> 00:35:23,206
But Mr. Kanebashi lent me that shop
when I left Doshi

470
00:35:23,476 --> 00:35:26,476
I absolutely want to help you

471
00:35:27,559 --> 00:35:30,605
I hope the Tatsunoya expands
and becomes very successful

472
00:35:30,630 --> 00:35:34,292
That place is the last remaining asset of the Kanematsu Group

473
00:35:36,510 --> 00:35:39,510
It seems that Boss Kanematsu's time in power will not last much longer

474
00:35:40,239 --> 00:35:45,871
With that old-fashioned brain, He cannot survive in this world.

475
00:35:46,329 --> 00:35:48,683
You speak quite frankly, don't you?

476
00:35:51,552 --> 00:35:53,800
That depends on the other person.

477
00:35:54,432 --> 00:35:56,324
I think you'll understand

478
00:35:57,359 --> 00:35:57,913
Why?

479
00:36:00,311 --> 00:36:05,504
What do ordinary people think when they see two
people drinking brandy like this in a nightclub?

480
00:36:06,087 --> 00:36:10,511
No one would ever guess that she's the
daughter of a yakuza boss and a gambler, right?

481
00:36:10,754 --> 00:36:12,098
In short....

482
00:36:13,049 --> 00:36:14,847
That's basically it

483
00:36:21,402 --> 00:36:22,426
Aki-san.

484
00:36:23,744 --> 00:36:27,378
Aki, why don't you take over as the second generation of Tatsuzo, the master carpenter, and start selling your services?

485
00:36:29,100 --> 00:36:31,009
You used to be a famous beauty.

486
00:36:31,831 --> 00:36:34,088
It's a waste for you to be stuck working at a small restaurant

487
00:36:35,399 --> 00:36:38,399
So Do you want me to sit down for the Tachibana group?

488
00:36:38,960 --> 00:36:41,960
I thought the job of a Doshi maker was something women couldn't do

489
00:36:43,180 --> 00:36:47,566
Women are weak-minded and emotional creatures

490
00:36:47,770 --> 00:36:48,894
Just like the Sally

491
00:36:53,360 --> 00:36:54,222
But you're different

492
00:36:57,960 --> 00:37:00,441
You always control men with a cool, composed expression.

493
00:37:01,170 --> 00:37:04,170
That shakes a man's heart and drives him crazy

494
00:37:04,840 --> 00:37:09,019
I have no intention of ever working as a gambler again

495
00:37:10,264 --> 00:37:12,860
We are willing to pay three times Tatsuzo's salary.

496
00:37:12,970 --> 00:37:15,970
I want to find happiness in an ordinary life

497
00:37:17,000 --> 00:37:20,589
I want to live a decent life, no matter how small

498
00:37:32,170 --> 00:37:34,480
I've thought that a few times when I was younger

499
00:37:35,780 --> 00:37:36,605
But Aki-san

500
00:37:37,720 --> 00:37:40,566
Ordinary people aren't as pure as you think

501
00:37:41,941 --> 00:37:44,300
Even if they are stupid or poor,

502
00:37:44,678 --> 00:37:47,027
They always have the feeling of superiority that they are better than a yakuza

503
00:37:48,169 --> 00:37:50,699
I've felt that way since I was a kid, and just you wait and see,

504
00:37:50,875 --> 00:37:53,875
I'm going to shatter the wall that discriminates between yakuza and ordinary citizens

505
00:37:57,870 --> 00:37:59,746
That's how I've lived my life

506
00:38:09,710 --> 00:38:10,676
Even at this store

507
00:38:10,700 --> 00:38:13,035
I employed a large number of ordinary people.

508
00:38:14,366 --> 00:38:20,996
I tried to make them realize that they were earning money thanks to the yakuza.

509
00:38:28,512 --> 00:38:29,121
Aki-san

510
00:38:30,183 --> 00:38:31,847
why don't you team up with me?

511
00:38:33,597 --> 00:38:36,972
There is an underground facility in the building that goes undetected by the police.

512
00:38:38,044 --> 00:38:42,308
We are building a modern gambling facility there, and we would like you to take control of it.

513
00:38:44,846 --> 00:38:46,831
I'll prepare a better apartment for you to live in

514
00:38:48,230 --> 00:38:54,316
I can't think the same way you do, nor can I live the same way you do

515
00:38:55,833 --> 00:38:57,206
How about a 2 million yen dowry?

516
00:39:00,010 --> 00:39:03,010
I'm going to marry a salaryman

517
00:39:04,090 --> 00:39:07,090
The other person is also aware that I was the daughter of a gambler

518
00:39:08,817 --> 00:39:11,316
I want to become a woman worthy of that person

519
00:39:13,940 --> 00:39:17,808
So, I guess I can't enter us then

520
00:39:19,020 --> 00:39:22,824
I've started to get kind of scared of you

521
00:39:24,040 --> 00:39:29,339
I'm scared of you because you're willing to do anything, no matter how terrible, to get your own way

522
00:39:38,257 --> 00:39:40,269
I've never actually killed anyone

523
00:39:45,035 --> 00:39:50,055
You would never do something so stupid that it would put you in jail

524
00:39:50,377 --> 00:39:57,073
Yes, You could take away their territory and force them to disband, or bankrupt them and drive them to suicide

525
00:40:05,089 --> 00:40:07,933
I wouldn't gain anything from
Tatsuo dying

526
00:40:09,035 --> 00:40:12,839
That's right, my father was a gambler

527
00:40:13,622 --> 00:40:16,622
and he didn't let you make money by cheating

528
00:40:19,260 --> 00:40:22,260
Let's have another drink and talk more casually

529
00:40:23,100 --> 00:40:26,100
In any case, please be aware of the situation regarding the Tatsunoya.

530
00:40:28,186 --> 00:40:29,792
I'm not giving up on you

531
00:40:49,738 --> 00:40:51,816
Oh, isn't that Masakichi?

532
00:40:58,692 --> 00:41:00,425
Don't you think that's strange?

533
00:41:01,177 --> 00:41:02,179
What do you mean?

534
00:41:02,203 --> 00:41:03,623
Tachibana's way of doing things

535
00:41:04,640 --> 00:41:05,636
After the events at the hanafuda

536
00:41:05,660 --> 00:41:08,456
he gained Chairman Chiba's approval and quickly formed the Tachibana-gumi,

537
00:41:08,480 --> 00:41:11,480
rising to the top ranks of the Kyoyu-kai

538
00:41:12,780 --> 00:41:17,046
But now he's extending his reach into the
Kanematsu-gumi's territory and targeting me as well

539
00:41:17,070 --> 00:41:20,070
I see, now that you mention it, it was a very smooth and successful career path

540
00:41:22,393 --> 00:41:31,511
I just can't believe that the noble Tachibana who risked his life to expose the cheating and the calculating Tachibana who has no sense of duty or compassion are the same person

541
00:41:32,637 --> 00:41:33,488
I figured out

542
00:41:34,229 --> 00:41:36,737
I think there must be some underlying reason behind the incident involving the Hanafuda cards.

543
00:41:36,762 --> 00:41:37,688
That's right

544
00:41:38,424 --> 00:41:40,920
It's a bit of a hassle, but could you go to Osaka for me? Osaka?

545
00:41:41,480 --> 00:41:42,105
Osaka?

546
00:41:42,860 --> 00:41:45,535
Tsukada, who had Dad rig the scam

547
00:41:45,880 --> 00:41:48,326
I think if we can find and capture that person,

548
00:41:48,350 --> 00:41:50,113
we might find out something

549
00:41:50,340 --> 00:41:54,269
Now that you mention it, it is strange that Mr. Tsukada has been gone ever since

550
00:41:54,690 --> 00:41:57,690
I just can't trust the man,Tachibana.

551
00:41:58,882 --> 00:42:01,058
I think there must have been some kind of trick involved.

552
00:42:01,199 --> 00:42:02,394
Leave it to me

553
00:42:02,686 --> 00:42:05,686
If I look for fellow gamblers, I'll find out where Mr. Tsukada is.

554
00:42:06,070 --> 00:42:07,176
I'm off now

555
00:42:09,973 --> 00:42:11,723
Come on,Hiroshi.

556
00:42:15,105 --> 00:42:18,105
Hey old man,These are mine.

557
00:42:21,699 --> 00:42:23,746
Hiroshi.

558
00:42:25,105 --> 00:42:26,801
Come on,Hiroshi.

559
00:42:31,996 --> 00:42:33,809
Come on,Hiroshi.

560
00:42:36,629 --> 00:42:39,246
The police have arrived.,Hiroshi.

561
00:42:52,269 --> 00:42:53,215
Hiroshi.

562
00:42:55,512 --> 00:42:56,512
You bastard!

563
00:42:57,982 --> 00:42:59,003
what do you guys think?

564
00:42:59,553 --> 00:43:00,613
Are you reflecting on your actions?

565
00:43:01,630 --> 00:43:03,613
Or are you staying another night?

566
00:43:05,440 --> 00:43:07,116
Are you even students?

567
00:43:08,069 --> 00:43:11,714
Don't you feel ashamed of yourself for fighting with yakuza?

568
00:43:13,453 --> 00:43:19,488
If they are left to their own devices like this, they will drop out of school and end up in the world of the yakuza.

569
00:43:20,565 --> 00:43:24,440
Parents should also explain things to their children and encourage them to be more self-aware

570
00:43:25,150 --> 00:43:29,472
I am very sorry for causing you so much trouble

571
00:43:30,810 --> 00:43:33,066
By the way, your damages...

572
00:43:33,348 --> 00:43:34,762
About 3500 yen

573
00:43:36,190 --> 00:43:37,356
Will you be sued?

574
00:43:37,441 --> 00:43:39,496
We won't do that if we get compensation.

575
00:43:40,160 --> 00:43:41,555
I'm sorry.

576
00:43:41,580 --> 00:43:42,496
It's fine

577
00:43:42,521 --> 00:43:44,410
It's good for young people to be full of energy.

578
00:43:44,435 --> 00:43:46,472
Hey, you don't need to say unnecessary things

579
00:43:48,559 --> 00:43:49,238
Hey.

580
00:43:49,418 --> 00:43:50,449
Bros.

581
00:43:50,635 --> 00:43:52,847
You idiot!

582
00:43:53,745 --> 00:43:55,863
You're causing trouble for ordinary citizens!

583
00:43:57,420 --> 00:44:00,420
I'm sorry to trouble you, Mr. Department Head

584
00:44:01,587 --> 00:44:04,133
just feed them these smelly bugs

585
00:44:04,260 --> 00:44:07,260
Heh heh, you're saying something really important, huh

586
00:44:08,179 --> 00:44:12,935
It seems that the Tachibana Group is being strict on the president's orders,

587
00:44:12,960 --> 00:44:13,896
but sometimes, my supervision lapses.

588
00:44:14,731 --> 00:44:18,318
We will compensate those we have inconvenienced

589
00:44:18,600 --> 00:44:20,796
Could you release the students?

590
00:44:20,969 --> 00:44:24,215
They are not dogs.

591
00:44:24,240 --> 00:44:25,662
Pardon, I apologize

592
00:44:26,140 --> 00:44:26,886
How are you?

593
00:44:26,910 --> 00:44:27,946
Are you okay?

594
00:44:27,970 --> 00:44:28,836
I'm fine

595
00:44:28,860 --> 00:44:29,787
Don't worry

596
00:44:32,606 --> 00:44:36,233
Hirose, please, I'm begging you, study seriously

597
00:44:37,526 --> 00:44:39,592
If you keep doing this, you won't just end up in college,

598
00:44:39,757 --> 00:44:43,724
you'll be just like those lowlife yakuza

599
00:44:44,082 --> 00:44:46,904
Sis, I don't want to go to university

600
00:44:49,350 --> 00:44:52,166
Even if I go to a third-rate university for you,

601
00:44:52,190 --> 00:44:53,779
I  won't be able to get a decent job

602
00:44:54,390 --> 00:44:58,376
More than anything, I want to work in a place
where I can rise to the top based on my abilities,

603
00:44:58,400 --> 00:44:59,553
even without a good education, and do things the way I want

604
00:45:00,840 --> 00:45:03,346
Hiroshi, what are you talking about?

605
00:45:03,377 --> 00:45:07,427
You know Tachibana-san, right?
I want to join the Tachibana gang,

606
00:45:07,569 --> 00:45:08,565
let me join

607
00:45:08,590 --> 00:45:10,647
Idiot! What are you talking about?!

608
00:45:11,360 --> 00:45:13,404
I'm not going to become a stupidly honest yakuza like my dad!

609
00:45:14,240 --> 00:45:18,092
I want to be a modern actor who makes tons of money like Tachibana-san

610
00:45:18,279 --> 00:45:20,147
Hiroshi...you....

611
00:45:20,186 --> 00:45:21,647
My father is a cheat and a bad person.

612
00:45:21,925 --> 00:45:23,545
It's ridiculous to resent Tachibana

613
00:45:23,854 --> 00:45:25,450
Tachibana is a great man!

614
00:45:25,490 --> 00:45:28,490
He's not the kind of Tachibana as you think

615
00:45:28,560 --> 00:45:30,006
Because even today...

616
00:45:30,030 --> 00:45:33,030
I think someone from the Tachibana gang spoke to the police on our behalf

617
00:45:34,010 --> 00:45:35,326
I want to do things my own way!

618
00:45:35,350 --> 00:45:35,946
Leave me alone!

619
00:45:35,971 --> 00:45:36,663
Hiroshi!

620
00:45:39,569 --> 00:45:41,196
That's impressive!

621
00:45:41,384 --> 00:45:44,384
It's amazing that you achieved so much success in such a short period of time.

622
00:45:44,510 --> 00:45:47,510
This is all thanks to the support of the chairman and you guys.

623
00:45:48,400 --> 00:45:50,826
Please come and visit us sometime in the evening

624
00:45:50,850 --> 00:45:51,678
Thank you

625
00:45:52,310 --> 00:45:57,272
I hope they continue to execute the Kyoyukai's business plan at this pace

626
00:45:57,592 --> 00:46:00,178
You can't make a living playing with dice these days

627
00:46:00,510 --> 00:46:02,156
We'll scrape together some money

628
00:46:02,180 --> 00:46:04,476
and we want to invest in your business.

629
00:46:04,500 --> 00:46:07,500
I bet the executives are all just old people

630
00:46:08,098 --> 00:46:10,248
Tachibana will have a tough time too

631
00:46:12,170 --> 00:46:14,046
We can't be laughing together, can we?

632
00:46:14,070 --> 00:46:16,006
You were always getting into trouble with the police.

633
00:46:16,031 --> 00:46:21,101
You can't even open a single Gamble place.
You should follow Tachibana's example.

634
00:46:22,132 --> 00:46:22,639
President

635
00:46:24,428 --> 00:46:25,420
Excuse me.,

636
00:46:33,592 --> 00:46:34,335
He's our president.

637
00:46:35,040 --> 00:46:36,014
I'm Sawai

638
00:46:43,110 --> 00:46:44,178
Do you smoke?

639
00:46:44,538 --> 00:46:45,249
Thanks.

640
00:46:56,289 --> 00:46:57,897
You want to join our gang?

641
00:46:59,232 --> 00:47:00,623
You're still in high school, right?

642
00:47:01,022 --> 00:47:03,038
But it's okay to just drop out of school.

643
00:47:04,843 --> 00:47:07,843
It looks like your older sister is going to get you into university.

644
00:47:08,308 --> 00:47:09,504
Did she give you that permission?

645
00:47:09,570 --> 00:47:12,570
I'm leaving home and becoming independent, so it's fine

646
00:47:14,840 --> 00:47:16,264
You shouldn't make your sister worry.

647
00:47:20,480 --> 00:47:23,967
I feel bad about what I did to your father

648
00:47:25,310 --> 00:47:29,706
I'm thinking of taking care of you since we're
looking to increase our gang's membership at the time

649
00:47:29,730 --> 00:47:31,615
So, can I have a sake cup then?

650
00:47:33,024 --> 00:47:33,951
A sake cup?

651
00:47:34,186 --> 00:47:34,647
Yes

652
00:47:37,034 --> 00:47:39,014
I hate old-fashioned things like that

653
00:47:40,830 --> 00:47:42,701
Parent and child exchange sake cups in front of the shrine

654
00:47:44,623 --> 00:47:46,219
If the boss says a black crow is white,

655
00:47:46,244 --> 00:47:47,834
the subordinate can't object and just agree

656
00:47:49,120 --> 00:47:50,536
Because they're doing things that are out of sync

657
00:47:50,560 --> 00:47:52,115
The yakuza will be driven out of modern society

658
00:47:55,040 --> 00:47:56,856
Do you own a suit?

659
00:47:57,435 --> 00:47:58,834
No

660
00:48:04,858 --> 00:48:05,569
Use this money to buy it.

661
00:48:06,124 --> 00:48:07,389
Don’t worry.

662
00:48:10,407 --> 00:48:12,240
Just take it

663
00:48:15,061 --> 00:48:16,663
Thank you very much.

664
00:48:19,154 --> 00:48:22,170
I'll put you the badges on the gang members' suits with my own hands

665
00:48:23,679 --> 00:48:25,285
That's my way of offering the sake cup

666
00:48:25,310 --> 00:48:25,819
Yes,

667
00:48:28,966 --> 00:48:33,647
we should do something to celebrate your sister's wedding

668
00:48:34,500 --> 00:48:36,139
Is the other person a company employee?

669
00:48:36,608 --> 00:48:38,615
He's a design engineer at Toyo Shipbuilding

670
00:48:39,669 --> 00:48:41,326
Hello, this is Moriya

671
00:48:42,010 --> 00:48:43,436
Yes, Aki-san

672
00:48:44,080 --> 00:48:45,631
Sorry to interrupt your work

673
00:48:46,310 --> 00:48:48,444
I'd like to ask for your advice regarding Hiroshi,

674
00:48:49,659 --> 00:48:50,765
if that's alright?

675
00:48:50,790 --> 00:48:52,176
About Hiroshi

676
00:48:52,200 --> 00:48:55,396
I'll stop by the shop on my way home

677
00:48:55,420 --> 00:48:57,826
It would be best to talk somewhere else.

678
00:48:57,850 --> 00:48:59,490
so wait for me at my apartment

679
00:49:00,630 --> 00:49:02,576
I'll be working overtime, so I'll be a little late

680
00:49:03,714 --> 00:49:06,714
I'll be back as soon as possible. The key is in its usual place

681
00:49:07,670 --> 00:49:09,616
Okay, then please do it

682
00:50:08,826 --> 00:50:10,764
Who?

683
00:50:16,921 --> 00:50:18,288
That's a pretty nice apartment, isn't it?

684
00:50:18,477 --> 00:50:19,411
What did you come here for?

685
00:50:20,640 --> 00:50:22,819
I came to see what your fiancé's life is like

686
00:50:25,220 --> 00:50:26,186
Please go home

687
00:50:29,249 --> 00:50:31,145
He seems to like ships.

688
00:50:31,170 --> 00:50:32,266
Please leave

689
00:50:32,290 --> 00:50:33,319
I'm going to call the police.

690
00:50:35,750 --> 00:50:37,576
What do you think you're going to do by calling the police?

691
00:50:37,998 --> 00:50:39,201
Go home soon

692
00:50:43,750 --> 00:50:45,553
I only finished elementary school, you know

693
00:50:46,710 --> 00:50:47,826
If you live a normal life,

694
00:50:47,850 --> 00:50:49,836
you'll end up spending your whole life in a slum

695
00:50:49,860 --> 00:50:51,561
Please stop spouting nonsense and go home

696
00:50:52,030 --> 00:50:52,893
Go home!

697
00:50:57,069 --> 00:50:59,420
I've been eating other people's food since I was a kid.

698
00:51:00,780 --> 00:51:03,022
I don't have time to be bothered with those loyal feeling.

699
00:51:04,591 --> 00:51:07,591
Those who resist will be relentlessly pursued and their very existence extinguished

700
00:51:07,933 --> 00:51:09,100
That's my way of doing things

701
00:51:10,080 --> 00:51:12,428
You have to make others unhappy too

702
00:51:12,549 --> 00:51:14,795
You are a despicable person who cannot live with peace of mind unless you do that.

703
00:51:16,842 --> 00:51:17,467
You think so?

704
00:51:18,388 --> 00:51:19,897
Ahhh what are you doing?

705
00:51:19,936 --> 00:51:20,905
Get your hands off of me!

706
00:51:21,733 --> 00:51:22,655
Get your hands off of me!

707
00:51:28,608 --> 00:51:29,835
What are you going to do with me?

708
00:52:10,374 --> 00:52:12,600
Who are you?

709
00:52:13,147 --> 00:52:14,569
I'm the one who love Aki.

710
00:52:15,444 --> 00:52:15,983
What?

711
00:52:18,561 --> 00:52:21,561
Don't believe what he's saying.

712
00:52:22,686 --> 00:52:23,733
Shut up.

713
00:52:29,420 --> 00:52:30,272
Mr.Moriya.

714
00:52:31,219 --> 00:52:33,053
You should give up on this woman

715
00:52:33,389 --> 00:52:34,171
What?

716
00:52:34,482 --> 00:52:38,194
She's not the type of woman to marry a salaryman

717
00:52:39,750 --> 00:52:41,998
What?
Cut it out.

718
00:52:43,678 --> 00:52:44,663
She's my woman.

719
00:52:53,303 --> 00:52:56,333
I can't get in the mood here

720
00:53:10,401 --> 00:53:14,084
Well, that guy's a yakuza named Tachibana

721
00:53:15,030 --> 00:53:18,053
Is what that man said true?

722
00:53:18,988 --> 00:53:21,030
That's a lie!
Why would I be with a guy like that?

723
00:53:21,303 --> 00:53:22,639
But you were....

724
00:53:23,092 --> 00:53:26,951
That man has set a trap to try and separate you and me.

725
00:53:46,561 --> 00:53:47,584
I'm so sorry

726
00:53:48,620 --> 00:53:53,319
It's my fault for making you feel this way

727
00:53:54,225 --> 00:53:56,465
It's because I'm still with them.

728
00:53:57,317 --> 00:54:00,282
It's not an environmental issue,
it's your mindset

729
00:54:01,149 --> 00:54:03,425
Why do you have a relationship with them?

730
00:54:04,897 --> 00:54:06,008
I find it unpleasant

731
00:54:08,586 --> 00:54:12,029
If that Tachibana guy was going to cause harm, why didn't you talk to me about it?

732
00:54:13,510 --> 00:54:16,510
There were plenty of other options, even if it meant relying solely on the police

733
00:54:17,670 --> 00:54:21,803
Toshio, I know you probably won't understand this,

734
00:54:22,890 --> 00:54:25,646
but there are some things that the police and the courts can't do anything about

735
00:54:25,670 --> 00:54:27,154
You're such a fool.

736
00:54:28,390 --> 00:54:30,636
You're only convinced of that

737
00:54:30,660 --> 00:54:32,397
because you're afraid of them

738
00:54:36,100 --> 00:54:39,100
I didn't want to tell you this, but...

739
00:54:40,260 --> 00:54:44,834
I think Tachibana might have been the reason my father committed suicide

740
00:54:45,905 --> 00:54:51,811
Knowing that I have my doubts, Tachibana is desperately trying to make me his own, please...

741
00:55:07,745 --> 00:55:13,459
Trust me, don't say anything for now,

742
00:55:13,900 --> 00:55:15,295
just support me

743
00:55:15,523 --> 00:55:25,577
I will surely cut ties with the yakuza world,
both in my heart and in my life, and come to you

744
00:55:30,961 --> 00:55:32,874
Hey Toshio

745
00:55:41,719 --> 00:55:44,054
I don't know what to do right now

746
00:55:45,510 --> 00:55:47,376
I just want to be alone,

747
00:55:47,400 --> 00:55:47,966
please leave me alone

748
00:55:52,068 --> 00:55:52,843
Please go home

749
00:55:54,765 --> 00:55:55,820
Get out.

750
00:56:02,890 --> 00:56:05,890
We're over now...

751
00:56:10,470 --> 00:56:11,624
Please, just go home

752
00:56:14,130 --> 00:56:15,241
Leave me alone

753
00:57:09,655 --> 00:57:12,655
Hey, did you hear that this area has become Tachibana-gumi's land?

754
00:57:12,680 --> 00:57:13,820
I didn't know that.

755
00:57:14,242 --> 00:57:16,609
what a laid-back person you are.

756
00:57:17,929 --> 00:57:20,484
But if this shop is going to be shut down,

757
00:57:20,509 --> 00:57:23,304
we'll have to think about where to go

758
00:57:26,850 --> 00:57:28,109
Welcome back!

759
00:57:28,195 --> 00:57:29,289
I'm home

760
00:57:33,606 --> 00:57:34,902
What's wrong?

761
00:57:36,039 --> 00:57:37,719
 You look really pale

762
00:57:38,458 --> 00:57:39,101
Where's Hiroshi?

763
00:57:39,804 --> 00:57:40,703
He's not back yet.

764
00:57:43,296 --> 00:57:45,225
So, Tome-san, can I have a drink?

765
00:57:45,929 --> 00:57:47,054
Just give me one glass

766
00:57:51,749 --> 00:57:52,523
Aki-san

767
00:57:53,700 --> 00:57:57,749
We're not really the best people to talk to about this

768
00:57:59,610 --> 00:58:05,757
Please don't hesitate to let me know if there's anything I can do to help

769
00:58:06,780 --> 00:58:09,266
Spit it out as if you'd drunk a whole glass

770
00:58:09,290 --> 00:58:11,038
It'll make you feel so relieved

771
00:58:11,940 --> 00:58:16,288
Thank you, Otome. It's getting late, so you can go home now.

772
00:58:24,304 --> 00:58:25,515
Excuse me.

773
00:58:26,328 --> 00:58:27,250
Good night.

774
00:58:27,305 --> 00:58:28,452
Thanks for your hard work

775
00:58:51,680 --> 00:58:56,843
You are like family to us; please don't look so sad.

776
00:59:10,335 --> 00:59:11,398
Thanks for your hard work.

777
00:59:12,027 --> 00:59:13,863
How was it?
 Were you able to meet Tsukada?

778
00:59:14,950 --> 00:59:17,546
I was running all over Osaka, but...

779
00:59:17,570 --> 00:59:19,140
I can't find any clues at all,

780
00:59:21,328 --> 00:59:22,304
Thanks for your hard work.

781
00:59:23,281 --> 00:59:24,312
so what's the matter?

782
00:59:25,121 --> 00:59:26,284
It's nothing

783
00:59:26,746 --> 00:59:27,906
it's about Moriya-san?

784
00:59:28,265 --> 00:59:28,898
It's fine

785
00:59:29,680 --> 00:59:30,523
It's all in the past now

786
00:59:30,931 --> 00:59:34,343
That's not good. I don't know why,

787
00:59:35,161 --> 00:59:37,195
It's not right for him to make you cry.

788
00:59:43,613 --> 00:59:44,523
Don't say anything more.

789
00:59:46,480 --> 00:59:49,480
It was probably something that ordinary people could never understand

790
00:59:50,890 --> 00:59:52,382
It's not Moriya's fault

791
00:59:54,490 --> 00:59:56,093
Let's have a drink

792
00:59:59,145 --> 01:00:01,273
You can't drink alcohol.
It's bad.

793
01:00:02,070 --> 01:00:05,646
As long as I have my father weighing on my mind.

794
01:00:05,670 --> 01:00:07,749
I can't possibly get married.

795
01:00:19,880 --> 01:00:21,655
I'm sure I gave you the money we agreed on.

796
01:00:25,100 --> 01:00:27,382
You were supposed to be in Osaka right now, weren't you?

797
01:00:27,960 --> 01:00:32,390
I've been feeling unwell since that happened

798
01:00:33,670 --> 01:00:35,498
I wanted to have a blast before setting off on my journey.

799
01:00:35,523 --> 01:00:37,546
But my luck was bad.

800
01:00:37,570 --> 01:00:39,986
I got scammed in Funabashi

801
01:00:40,010 --> 01:00:42,636
And then there's the usual,alcohol and women

802
01:00:42,660 --> 01:00:45,660
I was just hanging around with that woman

803
01:00:46,330 --> 01:00:49,330
When the money runs out, the relationship ends

804
01:00:51,468 --> 01:00:54,468
It's like saying that fighting a lot is a fate that never pays off

805
01:00:56,280 --> 01:00:57,296
How much do you want?

806
01:00:59,110 --> 01:01:00,796
1 million is a good amount

807
01:01:01,540 --> 01:01:03,124
I'll take 500,000 yen in cash

808
01:01:05,220 --> 01:01:07,023
I don't keep cash here

809
01:01:14,002 --> 01:01:15,484
Shall you meet with Chairman Senba?

810
01:01:17,790 --> 01:01:22,359
It seems that as people get older, they start to fall for that vibrant, youthful energy

811
01:01:29,160 --> 01:01:30,570
Well then, take care

812
01:01:38,312 --> 01:01:39,765
Do you want us to kill him?

813
01:01:41,316 --> 01:01:45,937
He's an idiot.
He came to collect the condolence money himself.

814
01:02:38,320 --> 01:02:41,281
What are you doing?
Follow him!

815
01:02:47,250 --> 01:02:49,375
Taxi!

816
01:02:54,523 --> 01:02:55,601
Welcome back.

817
01:03:15,250 --> 01:03:15,992
Tsukada-san

818
01:03:16,484 --> 01:03:17,484
Masakichi...

819
01:03:19,343 --> 01:03:21,281
I apologize for coming when you weren't there.

820
01:03:22,429 --> 01:03:24,468
I'm being chased by Tachibana

821
01:03:25,488 --> 01:03:27,499
I don't want to go anywhere

822
01:03:28,920 --> 01:03:31,920
Please, hide me until tomorrow

823
01:03:32,700 --> 01:03:36,851
Oh my god, I went all the way to Osaka looking for you!

824
01:03:37,400 --> 01:03:42,991
Oh, I have something I want to tell you

825
01:03:44,630 --> 01:03:45,812
I'm sorry

826
01:03:47,070 --> 01:03:54,195
I was so blinded by the 3 million yen that Tachibana casually offered that I forced Tatsuzo to set up a scam

827
01:03:55,249 --> 01:04:02,271
Tachibana, who distinguished himself in Hanafuda gambling, won the recognition of Chairman Semba and rose through the ranks.

828
01:04:03,829 --> 01:04:08,178
My father committed suicide out of a sense of responsibility.

829
01:04:08,908 --> 01:04:09,506
Damn it

830
01:04:10,916 --> 01:04:14,990
even if the trick is solved now, your father's life won't come back

831
01:04:16,400 --> 01:04:19,661
I never imagined Tatsuzo would commit suicide

832
01:04:20,660 --> 01:04:24,498
I'm so sorry, Aki-san, please forgive me

833
01:04:28,300 --> 01:04:30,639
I brought this on myself.

834
01:04:32,039 --> 01:04:34,506
I'm in this mess
because I'm being chased by Tachibana,

835
01:04:35,405 --> 01:04:40,654
Aki-chan
Do whatever you want... to your satisfaction

836
01:04:43,820 --> 01:04:46,820
The one I cannot forgive is Tachibana

837
01:05:04,300 --> 01:05:05,136
Who are you guys?

838
01:05:16,461 --> 01:05:17,810
Hurry up!

839
01:05:22,998 --> 01:05:26,444
Hey, that guy killed your father!

840
01:05:29,529 --> 01:05:32,529
Your father committed suicide because of him

841
01:05:32,850 --> 01:05:35,850
Stay down.

842
01:05:35,980 --> 01:05:37,029
Do it

843
01:05:38,131 --> 01:05:39,170
Get your hands off of me!

844
01:05:42,330 --> 01:05:43,428
It's the president's order!

845
01:05:44,389 --> 01:05:44,905
Do it quickly

846
01:05:52,233 --> 01:05:54,100
What's wrong? Hurry up and do it!

847
01:05:56,321 --> 01:05:57,596
You idiot!
Go!

848
01:06:20,058 --> 01:06:21,948
Tsukada!
You killed my dad!

849
01:06:22,237 --> 01:06:23,346
Wait a moment!

850
01:06:23,378 --> 01:06:27,229
That is a trap set by Tachibana.

851
01:06:28,886 --> 01:06:34,221
If you don't believe me,
ask your sister! Ask your sister!

852
01:06:56,307 --> 01:06:59,253
Besides the fracture in his right leg, he
only has scratches and no internal bleeding,

853
01:06:59,800 --> 01:07:02,112
so I don't think there's anything
to worry about

854
01:07:03,421 --> 01:07:05,112
Thank you very much.

855
01:07:05,223 --> 01:07:07,979
Well, since he's young, he'll probably recover quickly

856
01:07:08,004 --> 01:07:08,569
Well, take care.

857
01:07:14,097 --> 01:07:15,323
Sis.

858
01:07:20,807 --> 01:07:24,214
Hiroshi,there's no internal bleeding,
so there's nothing to worry about

859
01:07:25,055 --> 01:07:28,620
Tachibana wasn't the person I thought he was

860
01:07:29,705 --> 01:07:30,815
I was stupid

861
01:07:31,924 --> 01:07:32,870
It's fine.
if only you would understand

862
01:07:35,901 --> 01:07:37,140
I'm sorry, sis,

863
01:07:38,980 --> 01:07:42,346
I'll try my life again once I'm feeling better

864
01:07:43,930 --> 01:07:45,038
Hiroshi....

865
01:07:55,448 --> 01:07:56,605
I get it.

866
01:07:57,839 --> 01:08:00,206
He really made a fool of me.

867
01:08:01,995 --> 01:08:06,104
but now that Tsukada was killed

868
01:08:06,910 --> 01:08:09,536
It might be pointless to talk to Chairman Semba.

869
01:08:09,560 --> 01:08:11,737
But if I tell the truth....

870
01:08:13,237 --> 01:08:16,691
The chairman and the Kyoyukai won't be on our side.

871
01:08:18,870 --> 01:08:26,253
The chairman will surely keep Tachibana alive and suppress the truth, considering his own reputation and the interests of the Kyoyukai

872
01:08:28,172 --> 01:08:34,782
If you want to take down Tachibana, you'll have to be very determined, or you'll end up getting twisted in the opposite direction

873
01:08:35,991 --> 01:08:43,774
Rumor has it that a memorial gambling event for the first chairman of the Kyoyukai will be held in Kamakura soon

874
01:08:45,050 --> 01:08:49,751
Could you please let me participate as a dealer again?

875
01:08:51,550 --> 01:08:54,550
What am you supposed to do sitting there?

876
01:08:55,350 --> 01:09:00,673
I want to take revenge on Tachibana using the
same method that was used to frame my father

877
01:09:02,459 --> 01:09:04,285
Are you planning to set up a trick?

878
01:09:04,310 --> 01:09:04,548
Yes,

879
01:09:05,156 --> 01:09:09,212
I'll make it look like I've set up a trick to lure Tachibana in

880
01:09:11,427 --> 01:09:15,258
It's a clever trick to make people believe that a card that isn't a scam card is one

881
01:09:15,770 --> 01:09:21,011
I’ve heard from my father that it’s effective for people who have done it before.

882
01:09:22,840 --> 01:09:23,918
But Aki

883
01:09:24,410 --> 01:09:28,035
If you fail at that, it will become a huge problem.

884
01:09:29,500 --> 01:09:30,410
Yes I know.

885
01:09:31,879 --> 01:09:33,550
Don't do that, Aki-san

886
01:09:33,998 --> 01:09:35,605
You’ve finally managed to break free from the yakuza world.

887
01:09:35,692 --> 01:09:36,348
Lady...

888
01:09:37,380 --> 01:09:39,746
I hate Tachibana because he caused my father's death

889
01:09:39,785 --> 01:09:44,667
I am worried that something might happen to you.

890
01:09:45,762 --> 01:09:46,715
I am prepared.

891
01:09:48,518 --> 01:09:54,410
Aki, that's something you really can't do unless you risk your life

892
01:09:55,510 --> 01:09:58,510
Please let me sit on on just one more time.

893
01:10:11,670 --> 01:10:15,240
Masakichi, please read my eye count.

894
01:10:16,022 --> 01:10:16,506
4.

895
01:10:23,381 --> 01:10:23,967
2.

896
01:10:33,959 --> 01:10:34,490
6

897
01:10:41,756 --> 01:10:42,631
That's great!

898
01:10:43,724 --> 01:10:46,169
I'll be the dealer, so please be the customer.

899
01:10:46,412 --> 01:10:47,037
I get it.

900
01:10:55,818 --> 01:10:56,584
Ready?

901
01:10:59,333 --> 01:11:03,239
so wait, If you lower your eyes, it reveals that eye contact is taking place.

902
01:11:06,967 --> 01:11:08,383
That does not work

903
01:11:08,423 --> 01:11:09,939
The bottom of the paper is too wide

904
01:11:09,977 --> 01:11:11,208
Just as you are about to lie down, I can see the cards

905
01:11:11,921 --> 01:11:14,045
Now let's start over

906
01:11:16,826 --> 01:11:17,576
Ready?

907
01:11:23,610 --> 01:11:24,646
Your eyes are counting the cards

908
01:11:34,787 --> 01:11:35,490
Here we go.

909
01:11:41,153 --> 01:11:41,989
Amazing!

910
01:11:43,610 --> 01:11:45,836
Your intuition is getting sharper!

911
01:11:46,742 --> 01:11:50,576
All you need to do is remember the tactics and instincts for winning when it comes to placing your bets, and you'll be fine

912
01:11:51,634 --> 01:11:52,779
I can definitely trust you.

913
01:11:52,904 --> 01:11:55,732
When you're gambling, I can truly trust you.

914
01:12:02,235 --> 01:12:03,748
Let me do it again.

915
01:12:05,693 --> 01:12:06,342
Ready?

916
01:12:16,943 --> 01:12:17,709
What's wrong?

917
01:12:19,568 --> 01:12:25,006
It is a true honor to be of service to you once again.

918
01:12:26,590 --> 01:12:28,873
But this is the last time

919
01:12:29,640 --> 01:12:35,482
Masakichi, you've really done so much for me

920
01:12:36,022 --> 01:12:36,966
Oh....

921
01:12:37,424 --> 01:12:41,130
I and dad couldn't do anything for you either,

922
01:12:41,920 --> 01:12:43,349
but you helped me until the very end.

923
01:12:43,938 --> 01:12:47,442
I have no ability to do anything other than gamble.

924
01:12:48,264 --> 01:12:51,483
There is nothing else I can do for you.

925
01:12:52,089 --> 01:12:52,855
so even if I want to do something decent for you

926
01:12:52,880 --> 01:12:53,834
I can't remember any clever ideas.

927
01:12:54,810 --> 01:12:56,341
I am very happy just knowing how you feel.

928
01:12:57,246 --> 01:13:01,805
I cannot forgive anyone who destroys your happiness.

929
01:13:03,560 --> 01:13:04,623
Masakichi.

930
01:13:05,386 --> 01:13:07,840
I will be with you at the Kamakura Hanafuda event.

931
01:13:07,865 --> 01:13:10,294
Leave it to me in case of an emergency

932
01:13:15,370 --> 01:13:17,506
I'm no good at anything else,

933
01:13:17,530 --> 01:13:19,776
but when I sit on the bon, I get this crazy guts

934
01:13:19,800 --> 01:13:21,638
I'll do it tomorrow

935
01:13:22,244 --> 01:13:24,700
Masakichi

936
01:13:25,154 --> 01:13:29,833
As long as you are happy, that's all I need

937
01:13:37,987 --> 01:13:38,708
Thank you

938
01:13:41,037 --> 01:13:42,388
Now let's practice

939
01:13:43,100 --> 01:13:45,536
There are only 3 days left until the Kamakura event.

940
01:13:45,560 --> 01:13:46,302
Good luck!

941
01:14:08,960 --> 01:14:14,708
My older sister wanted to see Mr. Moriya when she got back, but she was worried about whether she would actually be able to meet them.

942
01:14:16,379 --> 01:14:18,161
Then I told her

943
01:14:19,070 --> 01:14:20,841
You have to believe in Moriya-san

944
01:14:22,177 --> 01:14:26,481
Moriya-san,
Are you still angry about my sis?

945
01:14:27,982 --> 01:14:32,122
My feelings for your older sister haven't changed

946
01:14:33,440 --> 01:14:35,886
There are some things about your sister's way of life that I can't understand

947
01:14:35,910 --> 01:14:38,910
I also suffered and was lost for a long time,

948
01:14:39,762 --> 01:14:43,302
but I started to think about what I would do if I were in your sister's position

949
01:14:45,180 --> 01:14:48,180
My sister is fighting desperately in a world I don't know about,

950
01:14:49,370 --> 01:14:52,370
but for no reason other than that I can't understand it

951
01:14:53,850 --> 01:14:57,209
I feel ashamed of myself for doubting Aki

952
01:15:00,005 --> 01:15:05,334
My sister said that today would be the last day she would ever be completely free from the world of the yakuza

953
01:15:20,600 --> 01:15:23,600
We will now move on to the traditional Japanese game of tehonbiki

954
01:15:23,930 --> 01:15:29,230
The 18 million yen, dealer is Sawai Aki

955
01:15:30,232 --> 01:15:32,818
I will do my best to serve you despite my inexperience.

956
01:16:00,694 --> 01:16:01,405
Let's begin!

957
01:16:01,720 --> 01:16:02,386
please

958
01:16:02,410 --> 01:16:03,896
Let's go in, let's begin

959
01:16:03,920 --> 01:16:05,045
Okay, let's begin.

960
01:16:10,116 --> 01:16:10,741
Ready?

961
01:16:33,178 --> 01:16:33,569
I made it.

962
01:16:34,131 --> 01:16:35,139
Come on in

963
01:16:35,873 --> 01:16:37,655
Come on in

964
01:16:37,998 --> 01:16:39,616
Come on in

965
01:16:41,397 --> 01:16:42,538
I made it.

966
01:16:42,967 --> 01:16:43,616
I made it.

967
01:16:43,967 --> 01:16:44,600
I made it.

968
01:16:45,084 --> 01:16:45,647
Ready?

969
01:17:06,944 --> 01:17:07,561
All set.

970
01:17:08,632 --> 01:17:09,967
Now, please bid.

971
01:17:10,120 --> 01:17:12,096
Please, go ahead, yes, go ahead

972
01:17:12,120 --> 01:17:14,520
Let's go in

973
01:17:15,544 --> 01:17:16,412
Now, please bid.

974
01:17:18,521 --> 01:17:20,404
I made it.

975
01:17:21,919 --> 01:17:22,599
Ready?

976
01:17:29,294 --> 01:17:29,701
2

977
01:17:46,793 --> 01:17:47,372
Ready?

978
01:18:04,941 --> 01:18:05,574
We're ready

979
01:18:06,240 --> 01:18:09,206
Go ahead, go ahead, go ahead,Now, please bid.

980
01:18:09,245 --> 01:18:12,245
Okay, go ahead. Is that right?

981
01:18:12,409 --> 01:18:14,091
Go ahead, go ahead, okay?

982
01:18:15,790 --> 01:18:17,916
Okay, it's done, I made it.

983
01:18:17,941 --> 01:18:18,675
Ready?

984
01:18:25,555 --> 01:18:26,253
Hold on!

985
01:18:39,862 --> 01:18:41,300
Can we change the Dealer?

986
01:18:42,080 --> 01:18:45,080
Do you have any doubts?

987
01:18:47,420 --> 01:18:49,331
This is something that's difficult to say in this setting

988
01:18:52,120 --> 01:18:56,626
If you have any doubts, I would like to ask you in front of us.

989
01:18:57,080 --> 01:19:00,080
If you're going to be so defiant, I can't just stay silent

990
01:19:02,330 --> 01:19:04,396
You can't get away with cheating in front of me!

991
01:19:04,420 --> 01:19:06,751
Please do not insult me.

992
01:19:07,129 --> 01:19:09,685
but if you have any evidence,
please show it to me

993
01:19:09,710 --> 01:19:10,977
The evidence is that card.

994
01:19:12,470 --> 01:19:13,767
The number on the card below is 4

995
01:19:14,579 --> 01:19:16,220
Mr. Kanematsu bet 4.

996
01:19:17,174 --> 01:19:18,438
If it turns out like this, you won't have any complaints, right?

997
01:19:21,150 --> 01:19:22,720
Are you Aki-san,right?"

998
01:19:23,949 --> 01:19:30,008
You're the daughter of Tatsuo, who committed suicide about six months ago, right?

999
01:19:30,240 --> 01:19:32,454
Yes, that is correct

1000
01:19:33,690 --> 01:19:37,993
Do you know why Tatsuzo died?

1001
01:19:39,130 --> 01:19:39,985
Yes, I do.

1002
01:19:46,750 --> 01:19:52,251
Tachibana, do you really have to raise that card?

1003
01:19:54,680 --> 01:19:56,095
This is what happened

1004
01:19:57,235 --> 01:19:59,657
I would like to conclude the matter once and for all

1005
01:20:00,707 --> 01:20:02,691
Aki, what about you?

1006
01:20:03,290 --> 01:20:06,290
Please go ahead

1007
01:20:08,480 --> 01:20:09,793
There's no other way,

1008
01:20:10,251 --> 01:20:11,360
let's check the cards!

1009
01:20:12,071 --> 01:20:13,796
We'll check the cards!

1010
01:20:13,820 --> 01:20:14,801
Please wait!

1011
01:20:20,059 --> 01:20:24,946
My father said that Doshi risk their lives for bon.

1012
01:20:26,429 --> 01:20:32,310
If the cards that were played in this match
were both 4s, as Tachibana-san said...

1013
01:20:33,080 --> 01:20:36,080
I will take responsibility just like my father did

1014
01:20:39,808 --> 01:20:47,746
But what would you do if even one of the cards was a different number?

1015
01:21:04,618 --> 01:21:06,847
I'll take responsibility as you said

1016
01:21:09,440 --> 01:21:11,082
Please, I beg you

1017
01:21:12,227 --> 01:21:13,684
Let me check it.

1018
01:21:23,364 --> 01:21:23,942
4

1019
01:21:30,966 --> 01:21:31,403
3

1020
01:21:34,780 --> 01:21:38,356
If you have any questions about the cards
please feel free to check again

1021
01:21:41,920 --> 01:21:44,806
As promised, Tachibana-san

1022
01:21:44,830 --> 01:21:47,268
Let's have you take responsibility just like my father did

1023
01:22:00,399 --> 01:22:01,407
You idiot...

1024
01:22:07,156 --> 01:22:10,489
If you're a man, you should take responsibility.

1025
01:22:13,785 --> 01:22:19,810
Tachibana-san?
Aki-san risked her life just like her father

1026
01:22:20,310 --> 01:22:22,116
Tachibana is still up to something

1027
01:22:34,240 --> 01:22:36,220
Put your feet down, Tachibana

1028
01:22:44,939 --> 01:22:46,103
Aki-san.

1029
01:23:48,773 --> 01:23:56,335
THE END

